e can note that A lacks evidence, making it a gap. We can suggest focusing on gathering stress resilience and decision quality for A and D, but we already have some for D (responds adequately). However we still need concrete examples. Also we need to update recommendation? Currently provisional vote is Candidate C. New info doesn't change that; still C strongest. We can reaffirm provisional vote for C, note that A lacks evidence on stress resilience and decision quality, making it less suitable. Also note D also lacks reliability and crew cooperation evidence, plus hot temper. So we can suggest next step: gather stress resilience and decision quality for D, maybe also reliability for A and D. But we already have reliability missing for A and D. So we can propose focusing on those.\n\nThus public message: summarize that A lacks stress resilience and decision quality evidence, while B has stress handling but crew cooperation issue, C strong on reliability, crew cooperation, stress resilience (calm in crisis) and decision quality (quick correct decisions), D has some but also hot temper and unknown reliability. Therefore C remains provisional best. Suggest next step: get any available observations on A's reliability and D's reliability/crew cooperation, and perhaps more on D's stress resilience and decision quality.\n\nNow produce final."}
